{
  "description": "The fallback guard (Pad's input protocol v2, Key shortcut): when a character isn't on the host's layout and the host would fall back to the key's US position (hid), it refuses combinations that close a window or quit. 'character' is what that fallback key types on the host's layout with the modifiers (null when the host can't tell; then the US position decides). 'modifiers' are literal host bits (shift 1, control 2, option/Alt 4, command = ⌘ on a Mac / Windows key on a PC 8). Mac: ⌘ with W or Q, whatever else is held. Windows: Ctrl+W, Ctrl+Q (it quits Krita, GIMP and Inkscape), and Ctrl+F4 or Alt+F4 (hid 61). 'decisions': the whole guard (guardShortcut) for a keyShortcut the host resolved: 'resolution' says whether the character was found on the layout, what the hid fallback types there (null = unknown) and the final literal modifiers. Named keys, bare hid positions and found characters are posted; a missing character falls back to its hid unless there is none or the fallback closes a window or quits, and then nothing is posted and the host reports key.unavailable with the character and the layout name. A key-up is always posted so nothing sticks. 'forHost': a stored shortcut's optional 'hosts' ({mac?, windows?}, each {key, modifiers} in the profile convention) gives a host its own key; shortcuts.forHost returns the shortcut that host uses, without 'hosts' (the shared key and modifiers where the host has no entry), keeping unknown members; 'resolve' is shortcuts.resolve for the same shortcut and host (literal). 'withHostEdit': shortcuts.withHostEdit stores an editor's change for one host: the host's own entry when it has one, else the shared key and modifiers; the other entry and unknown members are kept. Compare whole objects.",
  "cases": [
    {"host": "mac", "character": "w", "hid": 29, "modifiers": 8, "closing": true, "why": "AZERTY: the US Z position types W"},
    {"host": "mac", "character": "q", "hid": 4, "modifiers": 9, "closing": true},
    {"host": "mac", "character": "W", "hid": 26, "modifiers": 12, "closing": true},
    {"host": "mac", "character": "z", "hid": 26, "modifiers": 8, "closing": false, "why": "AZERTY: the US W position types Z"},
